## 3. Model Training Options: Local vs. Cloud

| Criteria | Option A: Local Training | Option B: Cloud Training (Colab / Kaggle) |
|---|---|---|
| **Hardware** | NVIDIA GPU (RTX 2060/3060/4060+) | Free NVIDIA T4 / P100 (Google Colab / Kaggle) |
| **Setup Time** | Quick (if CUDA/PyTorch already installed) | Zero local setup (Runs in browser notebook) |
| **Speed** | Fast (depends on local GPU) | Extremely Fast (T4/A100 hardware) |
| **Cost** | \$0 (uses existing GPU) | \$0 (Free Tier) or \$10/mo for Colab Pro |
| **Dataset Upload** | No upload needed (files local) | Upload dataset zip to Google Drive / Roboflow |
| **Best For** | Daily iterations & private datasets | Low-spec local PC or maximum GPU acceleration |

### Option A: Local Training Guide
Run directly from terminal inside `backend/`:
```powershell
# 1. Activate virtual environment
.\venv\Scripts\Activate

# 2. Install Ultralytics with CUDA support
pip install ultralytics torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

# 3. Start YOLO training (e.g. YOLOv10n or YOLOv11n)
yolo detect train data=data/dataset/dataset.yaml model=yolov10n.pt epochs=100 imgsz=640 batch=16 device=0 project=data/runs name=ingredient_model

# 4. Copy trained best.pt model to app weights
cp data/runs/ingredient_model/weights/best.pt app/engines/cv/weights/custom_ingredients.pt
```

### Option B: Cloud Training Guide (Google Colab / Roboflow)
1. Export dataset from local or Roboflow as YOLOv8/v10 format.
2. Open Google Colab notebook (GPU T4 enabled).
3. Run training script in Colab:
```python
!pip install ultralytics
from ultralytics import YOLO

# Load pre-trained model
model = YOLO('yolov10n.pt')

# Train model
results = model.train(data='dataset.yaml', epochs=100, imgsz=640, batch=16, device=0)

# Export model
model.export(format='onnx')  # Optional ONNX export for ultra-fast inference
```
4. Download `best.pt` from Google Drive and place it in `backend/app/engines/cv/weights/custom_ingredients.pt`. Update `settings.YOLO_MODEL_PATH` in `config.py`.

